        zeal-xonix change log

        1.4.1 - 2026-11-16

        * Add a short descending "uh-oh" sound when the player loses one life
          (the longer "oops" melody remains for game over).
        * Make the between-level prompt robust: a held or stuck key no longer
          blocks it, and it advances automatically after 30 seconds.
        * Speed up territory capture with a span fill that skips whole open and
          visited byte runs, a trail-byte bitmap, and byte-wide fill fast paths.
          The large-capture benchmark is about one third faster.

        1.4.0 - 2026-11-16

        * Add synthesized sound effects on the VideoBoard's four voices: a
          ping-pong blip when a ball bounces, a bell when territory is
          captured, a continuous buzz on levels with spiders, a sad melody
          after losing the last life, and a victory fanfare for a new
          first-place high score.
        * Stop gameplay sound before the high-score table and stop all sound
          when the program restarts or exits.

        1.3.0 - 2026-11-16

        * Show a top-ten high-score table when all lives are lost, ask for the
          player's name when the score qualifies, and save it as HISCORE.DAT
          next to the binary.  The file uses an XHS1 magic, XOR obfuscation and
          a 16-bit checksum; missing or corrupted files are ignored.
        * Wait for a key or 25 seconds on the table, then restart the program
          from the beginning (including the splash screen when enabled).
        * Extend the generated HUD font to the full A-Z alphabet for name entry
          and the high-score table.
        * Reduce memory use in the tile renderer so the larger program keeps a
          safe stack.

        1.2.0 - 2026-11-16

        * Add the 21-level campaign from the GDD: per-level ball count and
          speed, spider count and time limit.
        * Win a level at 75% captured territory; score uses the GDD multipliers.
        * Add a HUD with level, timer, progress and score.
        * Show a blinking yellow ">>> PRESS ANY KEY TO CONTINUE <<<" prompt on
          the second HUD line between levels, and wait for a key press.
        * Add an optional splash screen from assets/splash.zts, .ztp and .ztm
          with fade-in/fade-out; wait for a key or 25 seconds.  Missing files
          only produce a text-console warning, the game still starts.
        * Add the "--level N" launch option to start at any level.

        1.1.0 - 2026-11-16

        * Add land spiders: two diagonal enemies patrol the starting frame and
          all captured LAND; touching one costs a life.

        1.0.1 - 2026-11-16

        * Fix the multi-second freeze that followed every area capture: the
          capture now only examines the regions next to the trail instead of
          flood-filling the whole sea cell by cell.

        1.0.0 - 2026-11-06

        * Create new project
